July 24 (UPI) -- President Donald Trump on Friday ordered the Smithsonian's National Museum of American History to add signage warning visitors about "ideological" views in some of its displays.

Trump issued an executive order to add the signs based on a review of the Smithsonian's American History museum that he directed to search for ideological views related to social justice and "radical" changes to society.



